// SQLite corruption hardening (2026-07-29) -- live WAL-mode SQLite databases
// and their sidecar/conflict files must never be synced bidirectionally.
// Root cause of localized data/walkforward.db corruption. Do not remove
// without first addressing why these were excluded.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sync-conflict-*.db
*.sync-conflict-*.db-wal
*.sync-conflict-*.db-shm

// Point-in-time DB snapshots (recovery aside-copies, pre-cutover backups)
// don't end in *.db so the patterns above miss them -- found 2026-08-15
// while repairing data/walkforward.db (P1-11): both the fresh
// walkforward.db.corrupt_pre_p1-11_repair_*.bak(-wal/-shm) this repair
// produced and the pre-existing walkforward.db.pre_recovery_cutover_*.bak
// from the 2026-07-29 incident were sitting unexcluded, eligible for
// Syncthing to sync multi-GB static artifacts neither device needs.
*.bak
*.bak-wal
*.bak-shm

// High-churn, fully regenerable logs -- not needed for cross-device sync,
// and were themselves generating sync-conflict files.
logs/

// Dev tooling / build artifacts -- not needed for cross-device sync.
venv
.venv
.winvenv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.playwright_state
**/node_modules
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.cache
**/*.tmp
**/dive_smoketest*
out/dive_smoketest*

// Credentials / secrets must never sync between machines (B-4 fix, 2026-09-04,
// zcode-windows-infra session). .env hard-wires DB_PATH + carries tokens/passwords;
// .stockbit_token* is a live session credential. .env.example stays synced (template).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.stockbit_token*
